  "identifier": "whenyourdoctorsa0000unse_b1b9",
  "title": "When your doctor says diabetes : a guide to regaining control over your health and well-being",
  "creator": null,
  "year": 2010,
  "subject": "Diabetes -- Popular works",
  "description": [
    "xii, 419 p. : 23 cm",
    "\"A resource guide for people with diabetes. Describes different forms of diabetes; reviews diagnostic and monitoring tests; examines treatment options including insulin and other medications; explores eating plans and lifestyle modifications to prevent complications; reviews recent research; includes index and resource directory\"--Provided by publisher",
    "Includes bibliographical references and index",
    "UNDERSTANDING YOUR DIAGNOSIS -- Facts and myths -- Types of diabetes -- Gestational diabetes -- TESTS, PROCEDURES, TREATMENTS -- Diagnosing -- Understanding blood glucose levels -- Blood glucose monitoring -- How diabetes medicine works -- Oral antidiabetic drugs -- Injectable medications other than insulin -- Insulin -- Dietary suppliments -- STRATEGIES FOR MANAGING YOUR DIABETES -- What can I expect? --Working with a diabetes educator -- Working with a dietitian -- Eating for good health -- Tips of meal planning, cooking, eating out -- Diabetes and physical activity -- How weight affects diabetes -- Your mental health -- Illness affects blood sugar levels -- Away from home -- DIABETES COMPLICATIONS -- Preventing diabetes-related complications -- Bone health problems -- Eyes problems -- Foot and skin problems -- Heart and blood vessel problems -- Kidney problems -- Nerve problems -- Sexual and uologic problems -- Preventing and managing gastroparesis -- Tooth and gum problems -- handling diabetic emergencies -- RESEARCH AND RESOURCES -- Diabetes: yesterday, today, and tomorrow -- Pancreatic islet transportation -- Control and complications -- Diabetes prevention program -- Diabetes-friendly recipes -- Finding financial help for diabetes care -- Start a diabetes support group -- Directory of diabetes organizations"
  ],
